<!--
    ARM hard-float doubles passed to a callee nothing in the image describes
    (kuna_armfloatreturn.rs (opaque_callee)): an undefined symbol in a
    relocatable object, an import behind a PLT stub in a linked shared object,
    and a function pointer.

    armfloatargs_opaque_{arm,thumb}.o and armfloatargs_opaque.so (gcc -O2,
    recipes in armfloatargs_opaque.c). A d-register argument needed a stated
    or decoded callee contract, so a double the caller computed for such a call
    was dropped with the computation: `sink_d(d * 3.0)` printed `sink_d()`.
    With armfloatargs on, such a call scores the d-register as it scores s0
    and r0: scale_d, load_d, conv_d, two_d, mixed_id, indirect_d, moved_d and
    mixed_fd pass the doubles they write for the call. As for s0 and r0, an
    earlier call's result (chain_d), the caller's own entry d0 (forward_d) and a
    double the caller also stores (after_store) are not passed; the first two
    are limitations shared with every register. ign's body returns without
    reading d0, so call_ign passes it nothing. mixed_fd passes a float in s0
    and a double in d1; s1, the AAPCS-VFP back-fill slot, still holds half of
    the caller's entry d0 and is no argument.

    armfloatargs_opaque_split.o (authored, recipe in its .s) holds what such a
    call must not take: pieced_f, glibc's acospif shape, computes a float into
    s0 for invalidf while it writes d0 whole elsewhere, so the call's d0 is a
    piece of that float and the s1 the caller left; guard_d and guard_spin,
    glibc's drand48 shape, call __stack_chk_fail and spin, which never return,
    with the double they return still in d0. None of those is a double
    argument, and each function keeps its own prototype.

    armfloatargs_opaque_o0_{arm,thumb}.o (gcc -O0, recipes in
    armfloatargs_opaque_o0.c) pass a float in s0 and doubles from d1 after
    computing them in scratch registers that still hold values at the call.
    Those inactive trials (s13, s15, d7 and the like) are no later VFP
    arguments, so s1 stays the back-fill slot: o0_fd, o0_fp and o0_fdd pass no
    s1 and gain no float parameter for it.

    armfloatargs_opaque_noreturn.o (authored, recipe in its .s) is glibc
    strtod's round_and_return shape: guard_shared and tail_shared share one
    call to __stack_chk_fail between a path that leaves the entry d0 and one
    that leaves the result they return, so d0 there merges the two. A call
    that does not return takes no double.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "input-prototype", option armfloatargs. Pass 1
    (ARM object, armfloatargs off) pins the dropped arguments; passes 2 (ARM
    object), 3 (Thumb object), 4 (linked ARM shared object), 5 (authored
    object), 6 and 7 (-O0 ARM and Thumb objects) and 8 (authored no-return
    object) run the default.
-->
